# Day 25 - Sort Characters By Frequency

## Problem Statement
Given a string `s`, sort it in decreasing order based on the frequency of its characters.

The frequency of a character is the number of times it appears in the string. If there are multiple valid answers, return any one of them.

## Code

class Solution {
public:
    string frequencySort(string s) {
        unordered_map<char, int> m;

        for (char c : s) {
            m[c]++;
        }

        vector<pair<int, char>> p;

        for (auto i : m) {
            p.push_back({i.second, i.first});
        }

        sort(p.rbegin(), p.rend());

        string ans = "";

        for (auto &x : p) {
            ans += string(x.first, x.second);
        }

        return ans;
    }
};




## Time Complexity
**O(n + k log k)**

*`n` is the length of the string and `k` is the number of distinct characters.*


## Approach
This solution first uses an **unordered_map** to count the frequency of each character in the string. The character-frequency pairs are then stored in a vector, with the frequency placed first so that the vector can be sorted in descending order based on frequency. After sorting, the result string is constructed by appending each character as many times as its frequency. This produces a string where characters are arranged in decreasing order of their occurrence.


## Space Complexity
**O(k)**
